PART 4  does p0 control the attenuation as alpha = p0 + 2 p1 cos R?
        gradient rel-err at R = 0.4, sweeping p0
        p0      alpha        rel err      1-alpha^3
     0.000   0.921061     8.4252e-02     2.1861e-01
     0.200   0.936849     6.7693e-02     1.7774e-01
     0.333   0.947374     5.6580e-02     1.4972e-01
     0.500   0.960530     4.2599e-02     1.1380e-01
     0.700   0.976318     2.5683e-02     6.9376e-02
     0.900   0.992106     8.6042e-03     2.3495e-02

  p0=0 is the q=2 case (alpha = cos R). If the rel-err falls with
  p0 the extra level is buying a real knob; if it does not, the
  alpha model is wrong and q=3's only gain is the diagonal.
